Warrick, Yolanda,<br />
<br />
I have signed the closing memorandum. The Division will not recommend an ac=
tion against Vandergrift Rowe Investment Counsel premised on the 2011 under=
taking, and the matter is closed as to conduct occurring after December 31,=
 2012 on that theory. Nadine, this closes out TCR-2023-0521884 as referred.=
<br />
<br />
For the memorandum and for anyone who reads this file later, the reasoning =
in three lines. The firm gave the staff a written commitment on May 31, 201=
1 that was expressly limited to calendar years 2011 and 2012 and expired by=
 its own terms on December 31, 2012. The firm performed it, including both =
surprise examinations and both Form ADV-E filings. In December 2012 the sta=
ff confirmed to the firm in writing that it was not being asked to renew.<b=
r />
<br />
I want to be careful about how this gets summarized internally, because the=
 summary is what people will remember. The lesson is not that a 2011 examin=
ation letter defeats a later charge. It is that these letters mean what the=
y say, one at a time, and that two letters that look alike on the page can =
produce opposite results depending on a single clause. We closed one matter=
 this year on a commitment with no expiration and we are closing this one b=
ecause the commitment had one. The documents were recovered from the same a=
rchive, by the same search, in the same month.<br />
<br />
If Examinations wants to look at the post-2016 billing on its own facts und=
er the rule, nothing here prevents that, and the referral should be a new o=
ne rather than a continuation of this.<br />
